</div>
<h2 id="numbers">The Numbers</h2>
<p>Robinson's extension has a base value of $66.75 million over three years, with a maximum of $75 million if he hits incentives. That works out to a $22.25 million annual average — surpassing Saquon Barkley's $20.6 million, which had been the running back ceiling since his deal with the Eagles. Robinson also gets $51 million guaranteed, the most guaranteed money ever given to a running back on a non-rookie contract, including $37 million locked in at signing. The deal runs through the 2030 season.</p>
