<h2 id="next">What's Next</h2>
<p>Robinson is expected to ease back into practice over the coming week as the Falcons ramp him up ahead of the preseason. With the contract question resolved, all eyes shift to Gibbs and Detroit — and to how quickly Atlanta can get its newly-paid star integrated before games start to count.</p>
<h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">How much guaranteed money did Bijan Robinson get?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Robinson received $51 million guaranteed, the most guaranteed money ever given to a running back on a non-rookie contract. Of that, $37 million was locked in at signing.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Is Bijan Robinson now the highest-paid running back in NFL history?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Yes, by annual average. His $22.25 million per year surpasses Saquon Barkley's previous high of $20.6 million with the Eagles.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Will Jahmyr Gibbs's extension be bigger than Robinson's?</div>
<div class="faq-a">It's plausible. Gibbs was reportedly seeking a deal north of $20 million per year even before Robinson's extension, and Robinson's deal now sets a new floor for negotiations. Whether Gibbs surpasses it depends on how Detroit and his representatives value his receiving production compared to Robinson's overall workload.</div>
</div>
